    "body": "## Overview\n\nDeclare the QKV input mutable in both Qwen GDN core-op schemas. The convolution writes to this buffer in place; without the declaration, functionalization can lose that update.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Track input mutation for the standard and packed core ops.\n- Preserve kernel arithmetic, backend selection and existing output declarations.\n\n## Validation\n\nRebased onto `1ca0dfb9` on Oct 29, retaining the upstream GDN changes. Both CPU export regressions passed using the complete current GDN module, and applicable changed-file pre-commit checks passed. The C550 checks below are historical and have not been rerun on this head.\n\nThe CPU export regression fails both cases before the fix and passes both afterward:\n\n```bash\nVLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu .venv/bin/python -m pytest --noconftest \\\n  tests/kernels/mamba/test_gdn_input_mutation.py -q\n```\n\nPython 3.12.15, torch 2.14.1+cpu, using the target GDN module and updated dependencies over an older checkout.\n\nOn MetaX C550 (MACA 3.8.0.23, torch 2.10.0+metax3.8.0.7), a real native GDN layer failed `opcheck(test_schema)` before the fix with `Argument qkv_or_qkvz is not defined as mutable but was mutated`. Batches 1 and 4 passed afterward. Six convolution checks also passed, covering in-place/output parity, state equality, the sibling Z view and compiled/eager equality.\n\nThe packed fused-norm entry has CPU export and packed-view convolution coverage, but no full GPU attention run. No model was loaded. These checks used the target source in compatible environments, not a complete rebuilt main.\n\nApplicable pre-commit hooks passed, including mypy and CI test tethering. The existing Mamba kernel CI step selects the new tests.\n\n## Details\n\nThe convolution's output aliases its input, including the QKV slice of a packed projection. Declaring the input mutable makes the write part of the exported program's mutation outputs. Related #52190 changes Kimi KDA registration rather than these Qwen ops.\n\nAI-assisted implementation and validation; reviewed by the submitter.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
